# Build output. The .exe is ~15 MB and is rebuilt on every change, so committing
# it would put a fresh binary blob in git history each time and the repo would
# grow without bound. Attach it to a GitHub RELEASE instead: the repo stays
# small and users still get a download button.
dist/
build/
*.spec
*.exe

# Release bundles - assembled from the repo, not tracked in it.
*.zip

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Measurement output, if a copy is ever pulled off the printer to look at.
qidi_pa/
*.json
!thr_dict_*.json

# INTERNAL NOTES - not for publication.
# Working records, design memos and machine-specific detail (SSH paths, this
# printer's address). The published source deliberately refers to none of these,
# so nothing in the repo dangles when they are absent.
CLAUDE.md
NEXT_SESSION.md
PLAN.md
FINDINGS.md
HARDWARE_MAP.md
STAGE1_DESIGN.md
STAGE1_SEARCH_DESIGN.md
STAGE2_DESIGN.md
STAGE3_DESIGN.md

# Firmware reverse-engineering tooling - not needed to calibrate.
qidi_fw_dict.py
thr_dict_*.json

# Superseded, never installed.
qidi_pa_discover.py
